{"title":"Visible light","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Overview\">Overview</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Visible_light&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Overview\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Visible light is the frequency band in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electromagnetic_spectrum\" title=\"Electromagnetic spectrum\">electromagnetic spectrum</a> that is above infrared and below ultraviolet. It takes up less than a millionth of a percent of the spectrum, and is the only frequency range visible to the human eye. \n</p><p>Wavelengths of visible light can range from about 380 to 750 nanometers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Visible_light&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gamma_rays\" title=\"Gamma rays\">Gamma rays</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=X-Rays\" title=\"X-Rays\">X-Rays</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ultraviolet_rays\" title=\"Ultraviolet rays\">Ultraviolet rays</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Infrared_Rays\" title=\"Infrared Rays\">Infrared Rays</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Microwaves\" title=\"Microwaves\">Microwaves</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radio_waves\" title=\"Radio waves\">Radio waves</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018113716\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.009 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 6/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2